
Most calculations follow the common order as like on mathematics.
You can alter the order of calculations using parentheses



## Parentheses

Of course, we’re always allowed to use parentheses, 
which can change the natural order of calculation. 
Just like with arithmetic rules, subexpressions in parentheses are 
always calculated first. You can use as many parentheses as you 
need and we often use them to improve the readability of an expression, 
even if they don't change the order of operations.

